# Drift (DESIGN.md §9.3): what a faction does when a member's own acts carry them past their
# member tolerance (their rank's tolerance, if stricter).
load crates/cli/tests/fixtures/worlds/drift
# flag (the Guild): Nell is 60.00 away. Reporting a crime takes her to 4 / -9, 64.00 away.
act nell report_crime
# A theft brings her back to -1 / -12, 59.01 away.
act nell steal
# expel (the Ashen Circle): Ash is 40.00 away; a good deed takes him to 44.00. Out, at a
# cost of -20.00 with the Circle that spills +4.80 to the Temple.
act ash help_stranger
assert show character ash == ash — Ash — law 20.00, good -36.00 — Neutral Evil
# demote (the Temple): Ilse, a high priest 20.00 away, extorts and ends 26.02 away: past
# the high priest's 20.00, within the Temple's 45.00, so she becomes ordained.
act ilse extort
assert show character ilse == ilse — Ilse — law 28.00, good 54.00 — Neutral Good — member of temple (ordained) since tick 0
# Oren, an acolyte, ends 50.01 away: out on the lowest rung, so he's expelled.
act oren extort
# ignore (the Free Company): Brann drifts 1.46 from it, and nothing happens.
act brann steal
assert show character brann == brann — Brann — law -15.00, good -3.00 — True Neutral — member of free_company (sellsword) since tick 0
